# -------------------------
# 529 entries. The four sources below moved 1615 entries in all; 1086 of
# them were ALREADY here as well, so for those this was a removal from
# KEYWORD_WHITELIST and nothing was added. Counted after that overlap:
#   520  of the 1600 keyword entries of three or more words. A twenty-word
#        "keyword" is a term; these were only ever in KEYWORD_WHITELIST
#        because the substring bug fixed in 398aacf sent them there.
#     3  of the 8 broad keywords demoted from KEYWORD_WHITELIST. `wound`
#        alone exempted 311 terms and is what let a reporting standard
#        past the `reporting` keyword.
#     3  of the 6 terms taken off METHODOLOGY_BLOCKLIST -- domain
#        vocabulary that a methodology list would have deleted.
#     3  explicit exceptions the new precedence makes reachable:
#        `nacl 0.9%` (WONT_0000208) and `nacl 10%` (WONT_0000209),
#        which the noise regex rejects, and `degree of wound pain`
#        (WONT_0000415), whose only cover was the demoted `wound`.
